MR is nice, but the Eyes grant it without needing to be wielded.
That's quite valuable.  Needing to wield Magicbane for MR is a _major_
drawback, especially for roles that want to use a bigger, badder
weapon.  Your own repetition of the "don't unwield Magicbane" mantra
is evidence enough that relying on MB for MR puts severe restrictions
on gameplay.
Scaring things is okay, but wands serve the same purpose the few times
you need it (and fire/lightning are more reliable in terms of not
getting wiped out).  Outside of rogues, Elbereth isn't needed that
often (and even for them, taking things down at range + speed is much
more common than letting them get near and Elberething, your personal
love affair with the latter notwithstanding).
The spell points are very low impact, and it's a crappier weapon than
all kinds of non-artifacts (let alone a decent artifact weapon)
The big benefit you missed is the curse absorption, but that's mostly
a late-game benefit.

The Astral Vision is huge; you basically get a permanent light source
+ slotless MR, and while enlightenment isn't a huge deal it is nice
for IDing stuff early and more valuable than spell points and random
effects from Magicbane, IMO.

I stand by my position that DSM, the Eye, and the Eyes are all better
wishes than Magicbane, but MB is quite nice (and better than the Orb
of Fate, IMO).

